@startuml 07_Member_Banned

title 07. When Member Is Banned By Admin (Immediate Token Creation)

actor "Admin" as Admin
participant "Admin Client" as AdminClient
participant "Crypto Layer" as Crypto
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Vault KV" as Vault
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Other Members" as Members

Admin -> AdminClient: Ban member
activate AdminClient

AdminClient -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/ban-member\n{banned_user_id}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Verify admin permissions

Server -> DB: Remove member\nUPDATE members\nSET leave_date = NOW()\nSET banned = true
activate DB
DB --> Server: Member banned
deactivate DB

Server --> AdminClient: "Member banned successfully"
deactivate Server

note right of AdminClient
  No queued rotation
  Admin creates token immediately
end note

AdminClient -> Crypto: Generate new token
activate Crypto
Crypto --> AdminClient: token (plaintext)
deactivate Crypto

AdminClient -> Crypto: Encrypt token with group_key
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  encrypted_token = Encrypt(
    token,
    group_key
  )
end note
Crypto --> AdminClient: encrypted_token
deactivate Crypto

AdminClient -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/submit-token\n{encrypted_token, action: "ban"}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Verify:\n- Requester is admin\n- Recent ban action exists

Server -> Server: Derive new version name\n("v_1.3.4" -> "v_1.3.5")

Server -> Vault: PUT /conversations/{conv_id}/versions/{new_version}\n{encrypted_token, create_date, created_by}
activate Vault

Vault -> Vault: Store encrypted token
note right of Vault
  Cannot decrypt
  (encrypted with group_key)
end note

Vault --> Server: 201 Created
deactivate Vault

Server -> DB: UPDATE conversation\nSET latest_token_version = {new_version}
activate DB
DB --> Server: Updated
deactivate DB

Server -> WS: Notify all online members\n{conv_id, action: "invalidate_cache"}
activate WS

WS -> Members: Cache invalidation notification
note right of Members
  Other members will re-fetch
  conversation data and get
  new token version
end note

deactivate WS

Server --> AdminClient: "Token created and updated"
deactivate Server

AdminClient --> Admin: "Member banned,\nconversation secured"
deactivate AdminClient

activate Members

Members -> Members: Receive cache invalidation

Members -> Members: Clear local conversation cache

Members -> Server: GET /conversations/{conv_id}
activate Server

Server -> DB: Get conversation
activate DB
DB --> Server: {latest_token_version: "v_1.3.5", ...}
deactivate DB

Server --> Members: Updated conversation data
deactivate Server

Members -> Server: GET /token-versions/v_1.3.5
activate Server

Server -> Vault: GET /conversations/{conv_id}/versions/v_1.3.5
activate Vault
Vault --> Server: {encrypted_token, ...}
deactivate Vault

Server --> Members: encrypted_token
deactivate Server

Members -> Members: Decrypt token with group_key

Members --> Members: Can now decrypt\nfuture messages
deactivate Members

note over Admin, Members
  Result:
  ✅ Banned member removed immediately
  ✅ New token created without delay
  ✅ No scheduled queue (urgent action)
  ✅ Banned member cannot decrypt future messages
  ✅ Other members get new token automatically
  ⚡ Immediate security (no 5-minute wait)
end note

@enduml
